rag=false tok/s=13.8 | Q: Who was Hypatia? | A: **Hypatia of Alexandria** (c. 370–415 CE) was a renowned **philosopher**, **mathematician**, and ** astronomer** in ancient **Alexandria, Egypt**. She was the daughter of the philosopher **Aristarchus of Samos** and the head of the **Neoplatonic school** there. Hypatia made significant contributions to the fields of mathematics and astronomy, and she was also known for her teachings and her role in the intellectual community of her time. | Her life was marked by both intellectual achievement and political turmoil. She faced increasing tensions between the **Christian** and **Pagan** communities in Alexandria, culminating in her death at the hands of a Christian mob in 415 CE. Hypatia's legacy as a scholar and her role in the history of **Greek philosophy** continue to be celebrated.
